gth is size, index size is out of bounds. So maybe they intend that result[0] is something else (maybe null) and result[i] = this.get(i-1) for i >=1. So the assertion: For all i where 1 <= i < this.size(), result[i] == this.get(i-1). Also maybe result[0] is unspecified (maybe null). So we can express: \forall int i; 1 <= i && i < this.size(); \result[i].equals(\old(this.get(i-1))) . But note we need to refer to result array elements: \result[i] is the element at index i of the returned array. Since result type is Object[], we can use \result[i] (makes sense). Use .equals? Since elements may be objects, we could use == or equals. In prior examples they used .equals for query equality. Use .equals.

